The Brawl Pass is a progression system introduced in the [[Version_History#13/05/20_May_Update|May 2020 update]] that allows players to progressively earn rewards throughout the Brawl Pass season. The Brawl Pass replaced the old progression system, in which 100 [[Tokens]] would grant a [[Brawl Box]], and 10 [[XP#Star Tokens|Star Tokens]] would give you a Big Box.

The Brawl Pass consists of a free track, which is available to all players, and a premium track which requires a monetary purchase. By earning XP, players can unlock tiers that contain [[Gems]], [[Power Points]], [[Coins]], [[Credits]], [[Starr Drops]], [[Bling]], [[Boxes|Mega Boxes]], and Resource [[Vault Keys|Keys]]. It costs $8.99<ref name="cost">Price may be different in other regions.</ref> to unlock the premium track of the Brawl Pass for the season and unlock exclusive rewards, including season-exclusive [[Pins]], [[Profile Icons]], and [[Sprays]], as well as additional rewards such as Coins, Power Points, Gems, Credits, Brawler Keys, Skin Keys, and [[Titles]]. The Brawl Pass Plus costs $12.99 USD<ref name="cost"/>, and it adds more rewards to the premium tiers, including Buffie Keys and a 20% progression boost, as well as additional standard rewards such as Coins, Power Points, Gems, Credits, and Bling. 

After reaching the final tier of the pass (Tier 60), Bonus Reward is awarded for every 2800 XP. Animated gradient names are available for players who brought the Brawl Pass for the current season. Additionally, players will get one additional free item in the Daily Freebies section and can access the Brawl Pass exclusive Mega Quest. These are removed after that Brawl Pass season ends.

==Quests==
[[File:Quests.png|75px|left|link=]]
Quests are goals given to players that reward [[XP]] upon completion. There are different types of Quests: Small, Medium, Hard, and Special. Small Quests are unlocked after reaching 60 [[Trophies]], while the Medium and Hard are unlocked after reaching 230 Trophies. Some Quests are exclusive and can be progressed before the Brawl Pass is activated, but the reward will be given only after activating. Two Small Quests (for 200 XP) are given daily, and they reset after 24 hours. However, three Small Quests are given daily if the player has the Brawl Pass activated. Medium and Hard Quests are given for the whole season and new ones appear daily. Special Quests last for the entire season but can only be completed once. Some special Quests reward with [[Power Points]], [[Coins]], [[Bling]], [[Credits]], or [[Starr Drops]]. Other Quests are exclusive, and reward with [[Pins]], [[Sprays]], [[Profile Icons]], or [[:Category:Brawlers|Brawlers]]. A player has five rerolls that reset per week for the free or the paid version of the Brawl Pass, but only one Small Quest can be rerolled. Quests that are rerolled award the same number of XP but will not have the same objective nor the same Brawler/Event, and all progression on the Quest is reset.
